WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.500
Rub a balloon on a wool cloth.

2
00:00:02.550 --> 00:00:05.440
Hold it against a wall,
and it clings there.

3
00:00:05.490 --> 00:00:08.470
Odd, because the wall carries no charge.

4
00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:12.120
Yet a charged object
attracts any neutral object.

5
00:00:12.170 --> 00:00:15.830
Before the rubbing, the balloon
and the cloth were both neutral:

6
00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:18.570
equal numbers of protons and electrons.

7
00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:21.350
So where did the balloon's
charge come from?

8
00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:24.340
In this mission, you'll meet
the two kinds of charge,

9
00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:27.770
and the particles inside
every atom that carry them.

10
00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:32.800
Then you'll see why charge only ever comes
in whole-number multiples of one tiny

11
00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:33.790
amount.

12
00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:37.800
Your mission: find out where the
balloon's charge really came from.
